== Ruihan Xu



~~~
{}{img_left}{photos/bio.png}{alt text}{312}{230}

I am a student in Physical Science Division (PSD) of the university of chicago. I received my bachelor's degree in Mathematics and Applied Mathematics from Shanghai Jiao Tong university in 2024.  \n
My current research interests primarily include sampling (this broadly includes randomized algorithms on graphs, MCMC, and many sampling algorithms), machine learning (this includes LLM and many other learning theories) and a range of related topics in applied mathematics.

AI is reshaping academia, and I am actively exploring the broad topic of AI for Science:

- Check out [https://github.com/ruihanxx/medai MedAI], an agent-based project for automatically reproducing medical research papers and conducting autoresearch. Through this project, I am also exploring how contemporary scholarly publishing might be standardized and equipped with agent-facing interfaces to enable more efficient quality control, verification, and autoresearch.
- Check out my [notes.html notes] for mathematical observations and discoveries developed with AI in areas that interest me.

